n[1]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n \n(ii) \nExplain the term sustainable yield for a forest.\n[1]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n(This question continues on the following page)\n1020\n\n– 11 –\nTurn over\nM13/4/ENVSO/SP1/ENG/TZ0/XX\n(Question 3 continued)\n \n \n(iii) At carrying capacity the total biomass of the forest is 300 tonnes. Using the model \nin Figure 5, determine the value of total forest biomass which would theoretically \ngive the highest sustainable yield for the forest. Use appropriate units in your \nanswer.\n[1]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n \n(iv) Suggest one reason why harvesting the maximum sustainable yield of biomass \ncalculated from this model might not be sustainable in the long term.\n[1]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n(c) \nIdentify one method of reducing soil loss where bare soil is exposed after forest clearance.\n[1]\n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . \n \n. . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . .